Notebook[{
Cell["HypergraphRule", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"4f35277e-8adc-2b42-87bd-6a15dbd4c7ad"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"HypergraphRule", "[", 
    RowBox[{"input", ",", " ", "output"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"e9acf774-02f1-5541-82d5-489e23cc0519"],
 " ",
 "represents the rewrite rule taking the hypergraph input to the hypergraph \
output."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"01f42b15-3bb5-834d-8c5e-7f44ed923741"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"9ba5c5fd-3674-e54a-b4d9-df1d528e86c8"],

Cell["\<\
Either side may be given as anything Hypergraph accepts, and is converted; a \
side that is not a hypergraph gives HypergraphRule::hg.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4ab666f4-36ed-6143-8161-c3bc66a99be6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"rule", "[", "hg", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"66848665-2f86-5945-9146-eac1dc1f1a34"],
 " applies the rule, giving one event for every way the input matches. See ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphRuleApply", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"13052422-740e-3b48-8645-58c7b79b2215"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6c7df513-e656-8046-8d79-f43e00a33442"],

Cell["\<\
A vertex of the input that the output keeps is carried through the rewrite; \
one the output introduces is created fresh; one the output drops is \
destroyed. \"SharedVertices\", \"NewVertices\" and \"DeletedVertices\" report \
the three groups, read off the two sides by vertex identifier.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f5de6b23-f61f-0b40-83b4-5142b72350e6"],

Cell["\<\
Vertices correspond between the two sides by identifier, so the same name on \
both sides means the same vertex, and a name on the output alone means a new \
one.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"20633917-46ff-ae45-b685-e53d8f59af50"],

Cell["\<\
The shape follows the reference paclet this package grew out of, so that \
rules written for that one read the same here.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"7548151b-4492-3e4b-a25e-0927e71de2d6"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"8855341a-e183-524b-83a8-af5cbe94f5e4"],

Cell["\<\
Subdividing an edge: the two endpoints are kept, a third vertex is new.\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"f5503f13-0d6c-3844-8d44-bb9ebac6c0b7"],

Cell["sub = HypergraphRule[{{1, 2}}, {{1, 3}, {3, 2}}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c6c94e31-3368-174d-94ab-5e9a0734ac98"],

